# Environment variables are configured per service, not at the repository root.
# Each service reads only its own file:
#
#   backend/.env.example  -> backend/.env       server-side config and secrets
#   store/.env.example    -> store/.env.local   public browser configuration
#   admin/.env.example    -> admin/.env.local   public browser configuration
#
# Rules:
# - DATABASE_URL, JWT secrets and any provider credentials belong to the
#   backend only and must never appear in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle at build time.
# - Real values are never committed; only these .example files are tracked.
